# SASL Real-Time Sign Language Detection with GPU/CPU/Hybrid Training

This project implements an advanced real-time South African Sign Language (SASL) detection system using CNN-LSTM models enhanced with MediaPipe hand detection. The system now features **GPU-accelerated training** (10x faster), **CPU training** (universal compatibility), and **Hybrid CPU+GPU training** (balanced performance).

## **🚀 Quick Start - Interactive Launcher:**
```bash
python main.py
```
**Features:**
- 📊 **Performance Benchmark** - Test your system and get personalized recommendations
- 🚀 **GPU Training** - 10x faster training with NVIDIA GPUs (1-2 hours vs 10+ hours)
- 💻 **CPU Training** - Universal compatibility for all systems
- ⚡ **Hybrid Training** - Optimal CPU+GPU workload distribution
- 🎥 **GPU-Optimized Camera** - 25+ FPS real-time recognition vs 2-5 FPS CPU

---

## Features

### 🚀 Training Performance Options
- **GPU Training**: 10x faster than CPU (1-2 hours vs 10+ hours) with NVIDIA GPUs
- **CPU Training**: Universal compatibility for all systems (8-15 hours)
- **Hybrid Training**: Balanced CPU+GPU workload distribution (3-6 hours)
- **Automatic Optimization**: Smart batch size and memory management for your hardware

### 🎥 Real-Time Recognition Options
- **GPU-Optimized Camera**: 25+ FPS with <40ms latency for real-time responsiveness
- **Standard Camera**: 2-5 FPS CPU processing for universal compatibility
- **Live Performance Monitoring**: GPU memory, inference time, and FPS tracking

### Core Features
- **Real-Time Detection**: Uses a webcam to capture and classify sign language gestures in real-time
- **Hand Detection & Tracking**: MediaPipe integration for precise hand landmark detection and tracking
- **Enhanced CNN-LSTM Model**: Combines pre-trained CNN (ResNet18) with bidirectional LSTM and attention mechanism
- **Hand-Focused Training**: Trains on extracted hand regions for better accuracy
- **Custom Dataset Support**: Trains on custom datasets with automatic hand detection
- **Class Names Management**: Dynamic class name saving and loading for consistency

### Advanced Features
- **Performance Benchmark**: Test your system and get personalized training recommendations
- **Mixed Precision Training**: GPU memory optimization for faster training
- **Real-time Hand Visualization**: Live hand landmark and bounding box overlay
- **Video Analysis Tools**: Process existing videos with hand tracking annotations
- **Hand Region Extraction**: Extract and save hand regions for analysis
- **Performance Monitoring**: FPS tracking and detection rate statistics
- **Interactive Controls**: Toggle hand detection, reset buffers, pause/resume

---

## Dependencies
Ensure the following Python libraries are installed:

### Quick Installation
```bash
# Complete installation (recommended)
pip install -r 04_DOCUMENTATION/requirements.txt

# Minimal installation
pip install torch torchvision opencv-python mediapipe numpy scikit-learn
```

### Core Dependencies
- `torch` - PyTorch deep learning framework (with CUDA support for GPU training)
- `torchvision` - Computer vision utilities for PyTorch
- `opencv-python` - Computer vision library
- `Pillow` - Image processing library
- `numpy` - Numerical computing library
- `scikit-learn` - Machine learning utilities

### Enhanced Dependencies
- `mediapipe` - Google's hand detection and tracking library

### GPU Training (Optional but Recommended)
- **NVIDIA GPU** with 4GB+ VRAM
- **CUDA-compatible PyTorch** installation
- **Benefits**: 10x faster training, real-time GPU camera (25+ FPS)

**Alternative installations:**
```bash
# GPU installation (NVIDIA users)
pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
pip install opencv-python pillow numpy scikit-learn mediapipe

# CPU-only installation
pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
pip install opencv-python pillow numpy scikit-learn mediapipe
```

### System Requirements
| Component | Minimum | Recommended |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| **CPU Training** | 8GB RAM, Python 3.8+ | 16GB RAM, Python 3.10+ |
| **GPU Training** | 4GB VRAM GPU, 8GB RAM | 6GB+ VRAM GPU, 16GB RAM |
| **Storage** | 2GB free space | 5GB free space |

